15. Step 3: Understand Default Permissions
This is a very important concept. By default, a newly created IAM user has no permissions to access AWS services unless permissions are granted through an applicable policy.
For example:
•	Rahul can authenticate if console access is configured.
•	Rahul does not automatically have S3 access.
•	Rahul does not automatically have EC2 access.
•	Rahul cannot automatically create AWS resources.
This is known as implicit deny.
Trainer explanation: “Creating an IAM user is not the same as granting permissions. Authentication and authorization are two separate things.”
