18. Why Do We Need IAM Groups?
Suppose your company hires 20 developers. You create 20 individual IAM users. All developers need similar permissions. Should you attach the same policy to all 20 users individually? That is not an efficient approach.
Instead, create one IAM group and attach the policy to the group. Whenever you add a new developer to the group, the developer receives the permissions granted through that group.
 
