22. Important IAM Group Best Practices
•	Organize users according to job responsibilities.
•	Attach common policies to groups.
•	Avoid assigning permissions individually when group-based management is appropriate.
•	Review group membership regularly.
•	Remove users from groups when their responsibilities change.
•	Follow the principle of least privilege.
Remember: Users can belong to multiple IAM groups, and their effective permissions are evaluated across applicable policies and other AWS access controls.
Module 6: Principle of Least Privilege
23. What is the Principle of Least Privilege?
The principle of least privilege means giving an identity only the minimum permissions necessary to perform its assigned job.
Example: Suppose a developer needs to download files from an S3 bucket. Should we provide full S3 access? No. We should provide only the required read permissions on the required bucket.
 
