Module 7: Understanding How IAM Permissions Work
25. How Does AWS Evaluate Permissions?
Students should understand this basic flow:
 
Consider three scenarios:
Scenario 1: No policy attached
•	User tries to access S3.
•	No applicable Allow permission exists.
•	AWS denies the request.
Result: Access Denied.
Scenario 2: Allow policy attached
•	User tries to access S3.
•	An applicable policy allows the action.
•	No overriding explicit Deny or other restriction applies.
Result: Access Allowed.
Scenario 3: Explicit Deny exists
•	User has an Allow policy.
•	Another applicable policy explicitly denies the requested action.
•	Explicit Deny takes precedence.
Result: Access Denied.
Important technical point: AWS permission evaluation can also involve resource-based policies, permissions boundaries, service control policies (SCPs), session policies, and other controls. Students should learn these as they advance.
